# The fields of Flux's Kustomization (kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/v1) and of every type it holds,
# by the names flux build reads them under, at the modules the pinned flux records in its binary:
#
# flux: github.com/fluxcd/kustomize-controller/api v1.10.1
# flux: github.com/fluxcd/pkg/apis/kustomize v1.23.0
# flux: github.com/fluxcd/pkg/apis/meta v1.38.0
# flux: k8s.io/apimachinery v0.37.1
# root: Kustomization
#
# kustomize-controller's api/v1/kustomization_types.go and reference_types.go (Kustomization,
# KustomizationSpec, CommonMetadata, IgnoreRule, Decryption, PostBuild, SubstituteReference,
# CrossNamespaceSourceReference), fluxcd/pkg's apis/kustomize/kustomize_types.go (Patch, Selector,
# Image, CustomHealthCheck with HealthCheckExpressions inline) and apis/meta/reference_types.go
# (DependencyReference, LocalObjectReference, SecretKeyReference, KubeConfigReference,
# NamespacedObjectKindReference), and apimachinery's ObjectMeta (pkg/apis/meta/v1/types.go).
#
# flux build reads the Kustomization it is given with apimachinery's YAML decoder and
# encoding/json, which picks the document by the apiVersion, kind and name it decodes, and reads a
# key into a field when the key is the field's name or folds to it (ASCII letters without regard to
# case, U+017F as s and U+212A as k); it reads no other key. So every type is open: the checks
# refuse, at each typed position, a key that folds to a field's name without being it, and leave a
# key that matches no field to kubernetes-validate's schemas. One field a line: the type, the
# field, and what it holds, as in kustomization-fields; dirs is a list of Components flux build adds
# to the kustomization it builds, read from the directory it builds. spec.path names the directory
# built, which the checks read and check themselves before they build. status, an owner reference
# and the managed fields are refused: no tree holds them. TYPE * open marks a type as open.
